---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'ProfilePage',
    url: `${site.url}/about`,
    mainEntity: { '@id': `${site.url}/#person` },
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Raymond Ekpo is an Investor Narrative Specialist who helps pre-seed and seed founders explain why their company is worth investing in. He also runs Maneuver & Co."
  schema={schema}
>
  <PageHead kicker="About">
    <Fragment slot="title">I work on the part of a raise <em>that happens before the slides.</em></Fragment>
  </PageHead>

  <div class="wrap about rule-top">
    <aside class="byline" aria-label="Raymond Ekpo at a glance">
      {
        site.portrait ? (
          <img src={site.portrait} alt={site.name} class="portrait" width="640" height="800" />
        ) : (
          <div class="plate" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="plate-mono">R.E.</span>
          </div>
        )
      }
      <p class="byline-name display">{site.name}</p>
      <p class="byline-role caps">{site.role}</p>
      <dl class="byline-facts">
        <div>
          <dt class="caps">Works with</dt>
          <dd>Pre-seed and seed founders</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="caps">Raising from</dt>
          <dd>US and UK investors</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="caps">Also</dt>
          <dd>Founder, <a href={site.firm.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{site.firm.name}</a></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <ul class="byline-links">
        <li><a href={site.x.url} rel="me noopener" target="_blank" data-contact="x" class="link">X {site.x.handle}</a></li>
        <li><a href={site.linkedin} rel="me noopener" target="_blank" data-contact="linkedin" class="link">LinkedIn</a></li>
      </ul>
    </aside>

    <div class="prose about-prose">
      <p>
        I’m Raymond Ekpo. I help pre-seed and seed founders in the US and UK explain why their company is worth
        investing in: the thesis, the storyline, and the claims that hold it up.
      </p>

      <h2>Where this comes from</h2>
      <p>
        I spent several years studying how markets work, mostly by watching capable companies stall for reasons nobody
        inside them could name. That work became <a href={site.firm.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank"
          >{site.firm.name}</a
        >, the growth strategy firm I run. The job there is to establish what’s actually in the way and write it down in
        a form people can argue with.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same problem turns up at the very start of a company, in a different form. A founder knows the product, the
        customers and the market better than anyone, and still struggles to say why it’s an investment. That’s a
        different question from why it’s a good product.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="about-quote">
        <p class="display">A pitch deck is a positioning problem with a different buyer.</p>
      </blockquote>

      <h2>How I think about fundraising narratives</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Investors are buyers too.</strong> They’re buying a share of an outcome, and before they commit they have
        to explain it to someone else, whether that’s their partners, their co-investors or their own judgement. A
        narrative has to survive being retold without you in the room.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Clarity beats ambition.</strong> A smaller claim you can defend earns more trust than a bigger one you
        can’t. Overclaiming is the quickest way for a deck to lose an investor’s confidence, and they’re trained to spot
        it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The thinking comes first.</strong> If the investment case can’t be written as a clear paragraph, layout
        won’t fix it. So I write before I design, and every slide has to earn its place in the argument.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        I do the work myself. The person who reads your enquiry is the person who writes your narrative, from start to
        finish.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work in writing wherever it helps. A thesis you can read, forward and argue with is worth more than a call you
        have to remember. When a conversation would make the work better, we have one.
      </p>
      <p>
        And I don’t promise what I can’t control. Nobody can guarantee a raise. What I can do is make sure the investors
        you meet understand what you’re building and why it could matter.
      </p>

      <p class="about-next">
        <a href="/services" class="link">See the services and prices <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: 56px;
    padding-top: 32px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: 4fr 8fr;
      gap: 64px;
    }
    .byline {
      position: sticky;
      top: 100px;
      align-self: start;
    }
    .about-prose {
      margin-left: calc(100% / 8);
    }
  }

  .plate {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    max-width: 360px;
    background: var(--sheet);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--oxblood);
    color: var(--oxblood);
    box-shadow: 0 18px 40px -30px rgb(27 26 23 / 0.35);
  }

  .plate-mono {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(5rem, 9vw, 7.5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .portrait {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 360px;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: grayscale(0.15);
  }

  /* On phones the byline stays small so the writing starts sooner */
  @media (max-width: 999px) {
    .plate {
      max-width: 132px;
      aspect-ratio: 1;
    }
    .plate-mono {
      font-size: 3.2rem;
    }
    .portrait {
      max-width: 200px;
    }
  }

  .byline-name {
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 22px;
  }

  .byline-role {
    color: var(--oxblood);
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .byline-facts {
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    max-width: 360px;
    border-top: 3px double var(--ink);
  }

  .byline-facts > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .byline-facts dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-top: 0.25em;
  }

  .byline-facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .byline-facts a {
    color: var(--oxblood);
  }

  .byline-links {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .about-prose > p:first-child {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* No drop cap on "I’m": the apostrophe would drop with it */
  .about-prose > p:first-child::first-letter {
    float: none;
    font: inherit;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .about-quote {
    margin: 2em 0;
    padding: 20px 0 0;
    border-top: 3px solid var(--oxblood);
  }

  .about-quote p {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .about-next {
    margin-top: 2.5em;
  }
</style>
